# SENMA testing rules

## Focused validation first

Run focused tests relevant to the changed area before full regression.

Examples include:
- security suites;
- PJSIP suites;
- WSS/TLS suites;
- migration tests;
- readiness tests;
- backup/restore tests;
- controller authorization tests.

Do not rely only on exit code when the task requires semantic proof.

## Regression authority

The canonical regression suite is authoritative.

When required by the task:

```bash
make lint
make regression
make regression
```

Two consecutive full PASS runs are required.

A sequence such as:

```text
PASS
FAIL
PASS
```

does not count as two consecutive PASS runs.

Run again until two consecutive valid PASS runs exist, unless the task explicitly defines another rule.

## No repair between consecutive runs

Do not manually:
- restart services;
- recreate containers;
- repair ODBC;
- reload Asterisk;
- reset DB state;
- clean fixtures;

between consecutive canonical regression runs unless the regression itself owns that lifecycle or the task explicitly permits it.

## Test isolation

Fixtures must:
- have explicit ownership;
- use deterministic identifiers;
- clean themselves on success and failure;
- avoid deleting unknown/customer data.

Respect dependency/FK cleanup order.

## Runtime proofs

If a task affects telephony, use real runtime evidence where appropriate:
- registration;
- actual call;
- CDR write/readback;
- live Asterisk state;
- live TLS/WSS endpoint;
- AMI action.

Config presence alone is not runtime proof.

## Security proofs

For security-related tasks, validate the full matrix where applicable:

- unauthenticated;
- zero-permission;
- read-only;
- write-authorized;
- superuser;
- missing/invalid CSRF;
- direct endpoint access.

Denied requests must prove state remains unchanged.

## Canonical final gates

Unless the task says otherwise:

```bash
make lint
make regression
make regression
git diff --check
git status --short
```

Operational/release tasks may additionally require:

```bash
make doctor
make secrets-check
make migrate-check
make reconcile-check
```

## Result reporting

Use exact status:

- PASS
- FAIL
- BLOCKED
- PARTIAL
- NOT_RUN

Never turn an incomplete or interrupted run into PASS.

If a run is killed or interrupted, report it separately and rerun.
